{
  "description": "Shared test vectors for pass-token parsing of scanner and handheld/paste input (contract §6). The frontend parser (frontend/src/scanner/parsePassToken.ts) and the backend parser (app.security.tokens.extract_pass_token) must both return `expected` for every `input` (a token string, or null for invalid input).",
  "rules": [
    "Remove leading and trailing characters of the ECMAScript String.prototype.trim() set (WhiteSpace and LineTerminator: tab, vertical tab, form feed, space, U+00A0, U+FEFF, every Unicode Zs space separator, LF, CR, U+2028, U+2029). Nothing else is removed: the GS separator (U+001D) some handheld scanners append and U+0085 stay and make the input invalid.",
    "Bare token: the whole value matches [A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,128}.",
    "Otherwise a pass URL: it must contain no space or ASCII control character (U+0000-U+0020, U+007F) and fully match [Hh][Tt][Tt][Pp][Ss]?://[^/?#@\\\\]+/pass/?(\\?[^#]*)?#([A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,128}) - http or https (scheme case-insensitive), any host and port, no user info, path exactly /pass or /pass/ (case-sensitive), optional query, token as the whole fragment.",
    "Anything else is invalid. QR_BASE_URL and APP_BASE_URL are origins without a path, so every pass URL has the path /pass.",
    "Since Phase 12 a pass URL names its company in the query: {QR_BASE_URL}/pass?c=<slug>#<token>. The grammar is unchanged: the query is optional and is never read (the token is the whole fragment, and only the token decides), so the links of every release parse: with ?c=<slug> and without a query."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "bare token (token_urlsafe(32), 43 characters)",
      "input": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare token of minimum length 32",
      "input": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
      "expected": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare token of maximum length 128",
      "input": "Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-",
      "expected": "Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-Z9_-"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare token with surrounding spaces and a scanner CR LF",
      "input": "  Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A\r\n",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "https pass URL",
      "input": "https://visitors.example.com/pass#Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "http pass URL with port (local development)",
      "input": "http://localhost:5173/pass#Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "pass URL on a LAN IP with port",
      "input": "https://192.168.1.20:5173/pass#Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "pass URL on an IPv6 host",
      "input": "http://[::1]:5173/pass#Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
    },
    {
      "name": "pass URL from another origin",
      "input": "https://other-origin.example.org/pass#Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A",
      "expected": "Xo3_vK9-aQ2rT7mN4bL8cY1zW6eH5jP0sD-gF_uIk2A"
